# Artifact hygiene

Keep only what I need to review, in one known folder. Remove everything else you created.

## Evidence: one folder per run
- In a repo: `.artifacts/<run-id>/` at the root (gitignored). Outside a repo: `~/.agent-artifacts/<run-id>/`.
- `<run-id>` = `YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<slug>`, e.g. `20260930-2115-invoice-drawer` (sorts oldest to newest).
- Inside: `screenshots/`, `videos/`, `logs/`, and a `README.md` with one line per file saying what it proves.
- Create `.pending-review` in the run folder when you save evidence. Name the folder in your reply.
- pstack `verify-*` skills and `/create-verification-skill`: use `.artifacts/<run-id>/` as the
  evidence location they name. Their rule "cleanup never deletes evidence" still holds.

## Evidence lifecycle
1. End-of-task cleanup removes instances and scratch, never `.artifacts/`.
2. Evidence stays until I review it (I say so, or its PR is merged or closed). Then delete `.pending-review`.
3. Retention: keep the newest 5 runs. Older runs are deleted unless they contain `.keep`,
   or `.pending-review` is less than 30 days old.
4. Prune at the start of a new task, never in the task that made the evidence:
   `~/.config/chigozie-rules/prune-artifacts.sh --keep 5` (add `--dry-run` to preview).

## Scratch: delete before you finish
- Temp clones and worktrees go in `${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/agent-<run-id>/`; `rm -rf` it (`git worktree remove` for worktrees). Don't `cd` into it first.
- Test databases, containers, volumes: name them with the run-id and remove only those.
- Dev servers, watchers, browsers you started: record the PID at start, kill that PID. Never kill by name.
- Build output, downloaded media, generated fixtures, and screenshots or logs outside `.artifacts/`: delete.
- Helper scripts or files added only to verify something: delete, or move into the run folder if they are evidence.

## Never delete
- Anything you didn't create: my dev database, `node_modules`, build output I rely on, uploads.
- Evidence still pending review. Anything outside the repo, your scratch dir, or `.artifacts/`.

## Do / Don't
| Don't | Do |
| --- | --- |
| `screenshot.png` in the repo root | `.artifacts/20260930-2115-drawer/screenshots/drawer-open.png` |
| `/tmp/run.webm` left forever | `.artifacts/<run-id>/videos/checkout.webm`, listed in its README |
| `pkill -f vite` | `kill "$DEV_PID"` (the PID you saved when you started it) |
| `rm -rf .artifacts` right after capturing | leave it; prune later with retention |
| A test DB called `test` left running | `docker rm -f pg-20260930-2115` at the end |

## .gitignore snippet (see `~/.config/chigozie-rules/artifacts.gitignore`)
`.artifacts/`, `playwright-report/`, `test-results/`, `*.agent.log`

## Final reply
- Evidence: `.artifacts/<run-id>/` (N files), or "none".
- Cleaned up: clones, containers, servers (PIDs), temp files. Still running: what and why.
